  "description": "the 2002 Pro is made from\nFuji's new X-Fusion Alpha tubing. X-Fusion's aluminum alloy refuses to\nlose strength when it is welded. X-Fusion tubes can be made thin-walled.\nFat, light, thin-walled tubes like the Pro's downtube are strong and stiff\nbut still somehow compliant. An X-Fusion bike, a new Pro for example,\nwill be lighter and sweeter-riding than a bike made from yesterday's aluminum\nalloys.\n\nBut -- good material and thin walls aren't everything. You have to select\nthe correct frame tubes, frame size by frame size, for diameter and wall-thickness\ntaper. Make the right choices and the bike rides great: lively, stable,\nnot a bit harsh. Fuji's product people make those correct choices.\n\nA Pro is a great tool for your club's weekend hammerfests or the Paris-Roubaix\ncobblestone classic. The lovely Campagnolo parts and Vittoria tires will\ncope easily with either ordeal. The new tubing and carbon frame parts\nwill keep you fresh for the final sprint, at the city limit sign or on\nthe Roubaix velodrome.",
